            "end_line": 14,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Leading zero bytes must round-trip through Base58 encode/decode. // In Base58, each leading 0x00 byte is represented as the character '1'. final byte[] input = { 0, 0, 1, 2, 3 };"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 16,
            "end_line": 17,
            "line_count": 2,
            "preview": "final byte[] encoded = new Base58().encode(input); final String encodedStr = new String(encoded);"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 19,
            "end_line": 20,
            "line_count": 2,
            "preview": "// Two leading zero bytes → two leading '1' characters in the encoded string. assertTrue(encodedStr.startsWith(\"11\"), \"Leading zeros should encode as '1' characters\");"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 22,
            "end_line": 24,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Decoding must restore the original leading zero bytes exactly. final byte[] decoded = new Base58().decode(encoded); assertArrayEquals(input, decoded, \"Decoded should match original including leading zeros\");"
